  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transform 90 children&apos;s lives in a favela (Brazil)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Alagados favela is a 50,000 inhabitants urban neighborhood in Salvador de Bahia, one of the poorest of Brazil&apos;s large cities. It is infested by both human and drug trafficking. And of course the poorest children and teenagers are particularly vulnerable. With our program &apos;Being a Child in the Alagados&apos;, we offer secure and free school support. We serve 90 children between 6 and 15 years old, who receive tutoring, lessons in ecology, and training in care for others, along with 2 meals a day.</narrative>
  </description>
